---
description: Public repository guardrails and architecture boundaries
alwaysApply: true
---

This repository is PUBLIC. Git history is permanent and crawled.

Never write, in any file, commit message or comment:
- a brand, company, client or customer name
- a secret, token, key, password or connection string
- real data of any kind; fixtures use example.com, example.org or *.invalid
- a provider name inside core/ or domains/*/db or domains/*/domain
  (adapters may name their own provider)

Architecture boundaries, from DOCTRINE.md:
- the core contains no business word
- dependencies point down; a foreign key never goes sideways or upward
- a sideways read goes through a published view, never a foreign key
- when two domains need the same concept, it moves down, not sideways
- uniqueness keys live in the DDL, not in the caller
- delete policy by meaning: cascade = ownership, set null = attribution,
  restrict = guards what was already sent
- every index names, in a comment, the query it serves
- always qualify table names; never rely on search_path

Before any commit: run `node scripts/check.mjs`. Never commit on main.
Ask before adding a dependency, a core object, or a dependency between domains.
